; 14-orchestration.moritz - tutorial 14: orchestration, after Orchidea. A
; target sound is imitated by the players of an orchestra, whose sounds come
; from a database of instrumental samples: as chords whose summed spectrum is
; nearest the target's (mimetic), as a stochastic process of notes, never more
; at once than players (granular), or as that process following the shape of
; the target (morphological). The result is a score: a row an instrument, each
; note its sample, played and edited in the roll.
(patch
  (obj title comment "Tutorial 14 · Orchestration: targets, databases, the orchestra, the mimetic, granular and morphological modes" (pos 20 12))
  (obj t1 comment "orchestra holds a database of samples and the players; orchidea orchestrates with them, in the background (progress below), and sends a score." (pos 20 40))
  (obj t2 comment "Turn the audio on (the toolbar). Every step sends its settings to the one orchidea below (send t14orch); its score goes to the score box." (pos 20 58))
  (obj s1 comment "1. The targets: sounds in buffer~s. The bell (a static sound, one chord), the voice (a sound that changes) and the gong. Listen to each:" (pos 20 90))
  (obj b1 buffer~ t14bell archeos-bell.wav (pos 20 115))
  (obj b2 buffer~ t14vox Vox.wav (pos 200 115))
  (obj b3 buffer~ t14gong gong_c_sharp.wav (pos 380 115))
  (obj mx buffer~ t14mix (pos 560 115))
  (obj cmx comment "t14mix: the orchestra's sound (the chosen samples summed)" (pos 660 116))
  (obj l1 message "set t14bell, start" (pos 20 145))
  (obj l2 message "set t14vox, start" (pos 200 145))
  (obj l3 message "set t14gong, start" (pos 380 145))
  (obj l4 message "set t14mix, start" (pos 560 145))
  (obj lst message stop (pos 700 145))
  (obj s2 comment "2. The database: the samples of the instruments, a feature file in the *SOL layout named by its dataset: microsol comes with Moritz (oboe, horn," (pos 20 185))
  (obj s2b comment "   violin and cello, C4 to G4: small, quick); tinysol after Download TinySOL, fullsol once registered (Extras > Datasets...). info prints it in the Console." (pos 20 203))
  (obj band orchestra t14band microsol (pos 20 230))
  (obj inf message info (pos 160 230))
  (obj rdm message "read microsol" (pos 210 230))
  (obj rdt message "read tinysol" (pos 320 230))
  (obj rdf message "read fullsol" (pos 420 230))
  (obj s3 comment "3. The orchestra: the players, an instrument each (a number repeats it); Ob|Hn is one player who doubles; Vn+Vc two players paired (they sound" (pos 20 265))
  (obj s3b comment "   together in the granular mode). Without players, Orchidea's default orchestra of what the database has. The players come out on its last outlet." (pos 20 283))
  (obj pl1 message "players Ob 2 Hn 2 Vn 3 Vc 3" (pos 20 310))
  (obj pl2 message "players Ob Hn Ob|Hn Vn+Vc Vn+Vc" (pos 230 310))
  (obj plo prepend set (pos 470 340))
  (obj plm message "the players" (pos 470 370))
  (obj s4 comment "4. Mimetic, static: the bell is one segment; a genetic search finds the sounds, one per player or a rest, whose summed spectrum is nearest its own." (pos 20 410))
  (obj s4b comment "   Listen to the bell, then to the orchestra (t14mix, step 1); the score below has a row an instrument. population and epochs: more, nearer and slower." (pos 20 428))
  (obj m1 message "; t14orch mode mimetic, segmentation none, partials 0, population 300, epochs 300, run t14bell t14mix" (pos 20 455))
  (obj s5 comment "5. Mimetic, dynamic: the voice cut into segments where its spectrum changes (adaptive: against the flux's local median), a chord each, connected:" (pos 20 495))
  (obj s5b comment "   sustain holds a pitch the target keeps (one longer note), connection path takes the least melodic movement, dovetail keeps pivot notes." (pos 20 513))
  (obj m2 message "; t14orch mode mimetic, segmentation adaptive, ratio 2, timegate 250, partials 0, population 100, epochs 100, sustain 1, connection path, dovetail 0.75, run t14vox t14mix" (pos 20 540))
  (obj s5c comment "   another solution of a segment: choose segment n, or in the score's roll (step 8) a click on the segment's mark (\"2/5\"), its solutions by cost; report:" (pos 20 570))
  (obj m3 message "; t14orch choose 3 2" (pos 20 595))
  (obj m4 message "; t14orch report" (pos 170 595))
  (obj m5 message "; t14orch seed 7, run t14vox t14mix" (pos 290 595))
  (obj s6 comment "6. Granular: the orchestra as a process (run seconds): events a second (density), octaves (register), durations, dynamics, as numbers, ranges" (pos 20 635))
  (obj s6b comment "   (drawn at each event) or envelopes over time (at t value ...). Each event a note a player can play as recorded; never more than the players at once." (pos 20 653))
  (obj m6 message "; t14orch mode granular, seed 1, method random, just, density at 0 1 2 at 15 10 12, register at 0 4 4 at 15 4 5, duration at 0 1 2 at 15 0.1 0.4, dynamics at 0 0.1 at 15 0.9, run 15" (pos 20 680))
  (obj s6c comment "   the pitches by method: random, cluster (every pitch before any repeats), pivots, harmonic (a fundamental's partials, tuned justly), markov" (pos 20 710))
  (obj m7 message "; t14orch mode granular, method harmonic, fundamental C2, harmonicity 0.9, just 1, register 4 5, run 15" (pos 20 735))
  (obj m8 message "; t14orch method random, just, register 4 4" (pos 560 735))
  (obj s6d comment "   the saturation (the distance outlet): the share of the events that found every able player busy; report prints the events and each player" (pos 20 765))
  (obj s7 comment "7. Morphological: the granular process driven by a target: its density of attacks, its register, its loudness; at each event the free players' sounds" (pos 20 805))
  (obj s7b comment "   at its spectral peaks pursued against its spectrum, less what sounds; a note lasts as long as the target keeps its sound. The gong, then the voice:" (pos 20 823))
  (obj m9 message "; t14orch mode morphological, seed 1, min-density 3, run t14gong t14mix" (pos 20 850))
  (obj m10 message "; t14orch mode morphological, seed 2, min-density, voices 3, run t14vox t14mix" (pos 430 850))
  (obj s7c comment "   decision genetic: Orchidea's search at every event instead of the pursuit (slower; population and epochs as in step 4)" (pos 20 880))
  (obj m11 message "; t14orch mode morphological, decision genetic, population 60, epochs 40, min-density 3, run t14gong t14mix" (pos 20 905))
  (obj m12 message "; t14orch decision pursuit" (pos 470 905))
  (obj rc r t14orch (pos 20 945))
  (obj oi orchidea t14band (pos 20 975))
  (obj prog flonum (pos 20 1010))
  (obj cprog comment "progress" (pos 80 1011))
  (obj dist flonum (pos 160 1010))
  (obj cdist comment "distance (mimetic) or saturation (granular, morphological)" (pos 220 1011))
  (obj stp message stop (pos 560 1010))
  (obj s8 comment "8. The result as a score: a row an instrument in orchestral order, a note its sample with its dynamics, technique and cents (a target's partial" (pos 20 1050))
  (obj s8b comment "   off the tempered pitch). Play it; double-click it: the roll, edited as any score (Alt+Up and Alt+Down move the cents); write keeps it as a file." (pos 20 1068))
  (obj sc score t14score 2 @size 640 200 (pos 20 1095))
  (obj tr transport 60 4 4 (pos 680 1095))
  (obj sp message play (pos 680 1130))
  (obj ss message stop (pos 730 1130))
  (obj wr message "write ~/Documents/Moritz/t14orchestration.score" (pos 680 1160))
  (obj pa play~ t14bell 2 (pos 20 1315))
  (obj ch comment "the targets, the mix and the score, through a hall" (pos 160 1316))
  (obj sum +~ (pos 20 1345))
  (obj half *~ 0.4 (pos 20 1375))
  (obj rv reverb~ 0.3 2.5 (pos 20 1405))
  (obj out dac~ (pos 20 1445))
  (obj next comment "Next: tutorial 15, programming with Musil. Examples: 13 orchestration (Help > Browser), a feature each, the granular and morphological ones too." (pos 20 1490))
  (connect l1 0 pa 0)
  (connect l2 0 pa 0)
  (connect l3 0 pa 0)
  (connect l4 0 pa 0)
  (connect lst 0 pa 0)
  (connect inf 0 band 0)
  (connect rdm 0 band 0)
  (connect rdt 0 band 0)
  (connect rdf 0 band 0)
  (connect pl1 0 band 0)
  (connect pl2 0 band 0)
  (connect band 3 plo 0)
  (connect plo 0 plm 0)
  (connect rc 0 oi 0)
  (connect oi 0 prog 0)
  (connect oi 3 dist 0)
  (connect stp 0 oi 0)
  (connect oi 4 sc 0)
  (connect sp 0 sc 0)
  (connect ss 0 sc 0)
  (connect wr 0 sc 0)
  (connect pa 0 sum 0)
  (connect pa 1 sum 1)
  (connect sc 0 sum 0)
  (connect sc 1 sum 1)
  (connect sum 0 half 0)
  (connect half 0 rv 0)
  (connect rv 0 out 0)
  (connect rv 1 out 1))
